Subject: [candidate] preserve context-owned IOCTL buffers after IRP allocation failure

Applies after 0015. Buffered output can alias context->in_buff, including
the replacement buffer installed when output is larger than input. The
dispatch loop still owns that context buffer until IRP construction succeeds.
On allocation failure free only separate output and the replaced old input.
Keep the real STATUS_NO_MEMORY; do not transfer an unconstructed request.

--- a/dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/ntoskrnl.c
+++ b/dlls/ntoskrnl.exe/ntoskrnl.c
@@ -843,5 +843,6 @@
     if (!irp)
     {
-        HeapFree( GetProcessHeap(), 0, out_buff );
+        if (out_buff != context->in_buff) HeapFree( GetProcessHeap(), 0, out_buff );
+        HeapFree( GetProcessHeap(), 0, to_free );
         return STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
     }
